🚀 What is the EBS CSI Driver?

The Amazon EBS CSI Driver is a Kubernetes CSI (Container Storage Interface) driver that lets Pods in EKS use EBS volumes as Persistent Volumes (PVs).

Before the CSI driver:

EKS used “in-tree” volume plugins

These were deprecated and not feature-rich

EBS CSI Driver is now the only supported way to use EBS with EKS.
🧠 How the EBS CSI Driver Works

You create a StorageClass that defines:

volume type (gp3/gp2/io1)

IOPS

throughput

AZ

You create a PVC requesting that StorageClass.

The CSI driver:

Creates an EBS volume dynamically in AWS

Attaches it to the EC2 node running your Pod

Mounts it inside your Pod

=================================
✅ What is the EBS CSI Controller?

The Amazon EBS CSI Controller is the control-plane component of the EBS CSI (Container Storage Interface) driver, responsible for managing the lifecycle of EBS volumes from the Kubernetes control plane.

It runs as a Deployment (not on worker nodes) inside your cluster—typically in the namespace:kube-system or amazon-ebs-csi-driver


📌 Responsibilities of the EBS CSI Controller

The controller handles all operations that require communication with AWS APIs, such as:

1. Provisioning EBS Volumes

When a PVC is created, the controller:

Sends API requests to AWS

Creates the correct EBS volume (gp3, io1, st1…)

Applies tags, size, IOPS, encryption, KMS key, etc.

2. Attaching EBS Volumes to Worker Nodes

Attaches the created EBS volume to the EC2 instance (node) where the pod is scheduled.

Equivalent to calling:

aws ec2 attach-volume

3. Detaching EBS Volumes

When a pod is deleted or rescheduled:

The controller detaches the EBS Volume from the old node.

Ensures cleanup to avoid "VolumeInUse" errors.

4. Expanding (Resizing) EBS Volumes

If you increase the PVC size:

Controller modifies the EBS volume size

Nodelocal agent expands the filesystem

5. Snapshot Operations

If using VolumeSnapshotClass, the controller:

Creates EBS snapshots

Deletes snapshots

Restores PVCs from snapshots



